{
  "info": {
    "name": "Fernwood Heritage Retreat API",
    "description": "Fernwood Heritage Retreat - Hotel Booking System API collection (college capstone, requirement 16).\n\nSETUP - AUTH (cookie based, no JWT):\n1. Run the app: dotnet run. Note the URL in the output (http://localhost:5111 or https://localhost:7046).\n2. Set the collection variable baseUrl to that URL.\n3. Log in on the website in your browser (customer account).\n4. In Postman, click Cookies, add a cookie for the app domain: name .AspNetCore.Cookies, value copied from browser DevTools > Application > Cookies. (Login POST needs an antiforgery token, so a raw Postman login request will fail with 400 - use the browser cookie instead.)\n\nRUN ORDER: Rooms folder first, then Bookings Create -> Payments Pay -> Bookings Get by Id -> Bookings Cancel. Create Booking saves bookingId automatically.\n\nNOTE: Search/Create dates in this collection are 23-25 Nov 2026. If those dates have passed, change them to future dates.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5111"
    },
    {
      "key": "bookingId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "bookingRef",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
